column17:
The automated property generators are just syntactic sugar.  At the moment, if I want a property that's settable inside and out I can can type:<p><pre><code>  public string MyString{set;get;}
</code></pre>
In order to do the same with an immutable property requires a fair bit more code.<p><pre><code>  private readonly string myString;
  public string MyString
  {
    get
      {
         return myString;
      }
  }
</code></pre>
Replacing all of that with<p><pre><code>  public readonly string MyString{get;set;}
</code></pre>
would be handy, and work with the way the language currently does.
